# Does the equality-substitution family survive the eq_subst ban?
#
# IFOL.eq_reflection (a = b ==> a == b) is cited 16,431 times -- 16% of ALL IFOL
# citations -- and IFOL.subst (a = b ==> P(a) ==> P(b)) another 1,657. Neither can
# be a kernel over uninterpreted parameters: deriving P(b) from P(a) IS eq_subst.
#
# The question this probe settles: does §7's parameter-or-hypothesis rule rescue
# them? I.e. are they parametric ONCE the congruence they need is a hypothesis?
#
# Under S1 a term of type i is a unary relation, so the two equalities are:
#     object   a = b   ->  forall x y. A(x) -> B(y) -> eq(x,y)
#     meta     a == b  ->  forall r. set(r) -> (A(r) <-> B(r))     relation ext.
# eq_reflection is then exactly: object equality => relation extensionality.
# Base: Extensionality ALONE. Dropping members_are_sets or elem_first_subst
# leaves this green; dropping extensionality does not (it is what eq_symm needs).
# That is the point, not an economy: a parametric kernel's congruence is
# HYPOTHETICAL, so the atom-level substitution axioms (axiom 2, and axiom 3's
# <- direction) are consumed by whatever DISCHARGES the hypothesis -- the
# constant table or Compiler B -- never by the kernel itself.
axiom extensionality: forall A. forall B. (eq(A,B) <-> (forall u. (elem(u,A) <-> elem(u,B))))

claim eq_refl: forall A. eq(A,A)
claim eq_symm: forall A. forall B. (eq(A,B) -> eq(B,A))

# eq_reflection, parametric in the two RENDERINGS A and B.
# Hypotheses, in order: EX(A), EX(B), result-CONG(A), result-CONG(B), the object
# equation.  Note UNIQ is NOT needed -- only existence and congruence.
schema eq_reflection_rel [A(1), B(1)]: ((exists v. (set(v) & A(v))) -> ((exists v. (set(v) & B(v))) -> ((forall r. forall s. (set(r) -> (set(s) -> (eq(r,s) -> (A(r) -> A(s)))))) -> ((forall r. forall s. (set(r) -> (set(s) -> (eq(r,s) -> (B(r) -> B(s)))))) -> ((forall x. forall y. (set(x) -> (set(y) -> (A(x) -> (B(y) -> eq(x,y)))))) -> (forall r. (set(r) -> (A(r) <-> B(r)))))))))

# IFOL.subst, parametric in P once CONG(P) is a hypothesis. This is the shape
# Compiler B must discharge per concrete formula.
schema subst_rel [P(1)]: ((forall x. forall y. (set(x) -> (set(y) -> (eq(x,y) -> (P(x) -> P(y)))))) -> (forall a. forall b. (set(a) -> (set(b) -> (eq(a,b) -> (P(a) -> P(b)))))))
